                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238244348",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199557621541",
                            "num_reviews": 8,
                            "playtime_forever": 306,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 306,
                            "last_played": 1792369640
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have mixed feelings on this port. I ultimately gave it a positive review because I do think it's worth owning and playing.\n\nThe Last Blade itself is an incredible experience:\n- The gameplay is fun. It isn't overly complicated but it has a lot of depth the more time you spend playing it.\n- The characters are cool. No two characters feel or play the same. Everyone has their own unique personality quirks too.\n- The art style and overall presentation are wonderful. The sprites and stages look excellent.\n\nThe problems this port has:\n- Some bugs that can crash the game. Simple to fix but still a nuisance.\n- Move List menus that aren't easy to navigate. It's difficult to describe how they work but they're a chore to browse through.\n- 9 credits for arcade mode that cannot be refilled during a single run. Maybe they wanted the arcade achievements to mean something? It's a really weird inclusion.\n\nAll in all, a fun game, but not the most pleasing port.",
